WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.980
<b>Proof of Humanity</b>

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:14.610
Damn that Beta. Just how big is he gonna get?

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:19.390
He can change forms at will 
and merge with other matter to grow in size.

00:00:19.390 --> 00:00:21.680
But how can he do that?

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:24.200
That's Beta's own ability.

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:30.030
The ability the brain resting
within Number 00 Beta possesses

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:32.760
as a metal organism.

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:34.940
What? A "metal organism"?

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:37.140
Auctioneer!

00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:41.510
It's okay.

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:45.110
I knew I would be killed.

00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:49.830
That is why I made a clone.

00:00:51.350 --> 00:00:53.390
Is that so?

00:00:53.390 --> 00:00:58.680
If you've inherited Bro's memories, 
there's a ton of stuff I wanna ask you.

00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:00.540
But before that...

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:07.080
I'm gonna go finish the job 
I left undone that day!

00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:28.350
Here he comes.

00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:29.620
But...

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:31.790
see how you like this!

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:40.960
I assume you were aiming for my brain,

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:44.760
but what makes you think I'd put it 
in such an obvious place?

00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:46.810
Shit!

00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:49.020
You need more firepower.

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:51.100
We should get out of here for now!

00:01:58.520 --> 00:02:01.220
He has us right where he wants us!

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:03.100
Can't you use that thing yet?

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:11.080
Number 11 takes a while 
to recharge between shots.

00:02:13.370 --> 00:02:18.400
But didn't he fire off multiple shots 
in succession during the Tokyo Attack?

00:02:18.810 --> 00:02:24.650
Number 11, the palm EX-ARM which
can produce supergravitional spaces,

00:02:24.650 --> 00:02:32.300
performs to its potential only when paired 
with its generator, Number 12, the arm.

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:37.880
But Number 12 is currently missing.

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:42.640
And without the generator, Number
11 is effective only over a two-kilometer range.

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:47.470
So, how long until you can use it again?

00:02:47.870 --> 00:02:51.920
Around fifteen minutes, and Beta knows that.

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:54.820
He'll definitely try 
to finish us off in that time.

00:02:57.270 --> 00:03:00.860
Beta's tentacles? How'd they get here?!

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:04.120
Watch out, Akira!

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:07.290
Beta's rapidly absorbing
everything around him!

00:03:07.290 --> 00:03:12.120
He's merging with the stadium... 
No, with the entire Megafloat!

00:03:21.270 --> 00:03:22.260
What?

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:30.630
You fool!

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:34.240
Wait, is this entire building a part of him?

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:35.400
Look out!

00:05:19.940 --> 00:05:22.090
Did Akira just get swallowed whole?!

00:05:22.090 --> 00:05:24.590
You can't be serious!

00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:27.890
Wait, something seems off about Beta.

00:05:37.070 --> 00:05:39.560
Come in, Akira! Are you okay?!

00:05:39.560 --> 00:05:41.580
<i>Yeah, somehow.</i>

00:05:41.580 --> 00:05:43.030
And Auctioneer?

00:05:43.780 --> 00:05:49.140
Sorry, we were split up 
right after Beta ate us. I'm alone now.

00:05:50.470 --> 00:05:53.660
Number 11...

00:05:53.660 --> 00:05:57.190
Number 11!

00:05:59.640 --> 00:06:01.180
Beta!

00:06:01.180 --> 00:06:02.120
Die.

00:06:04.790 --> 00:06:06.550
Grab on, Akira!

00:06:12.630 --> 00:06:13.880
Thanks.

00:06:20.230 --> 00:06:22.670
That's 40 percent of the Tokyo Megafloat.

00:06:22.670 --> 00:06:25.200
Beta's diameter has grown 
past five kilometers now.

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:26.780
And he's still getting bigger.

00:06:29.350 --> 00:06:30.700
What a disaster.

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:37.980
Wh-Where are you all going?

00:06:37.980 --> 00:06:40.800
We're evacuating 
to the emergency bunker in Tachikawa.

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:44.040
Evacuating? You're just going 
to run away from this?!

00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:47.210
Japan can recover as long as we're around.

00:06:47.210 --> 00:06:50.510
Ensuring the Restoration Bloc's survival 
is of the utmost priority right now.

00:06:50.880 --> 00:06:56.010
A-Are you kidding me? Who do you think 
caused this mess in the first place?!

00:06:56.010 --> 00:06:58.220
Hold it! Don't run away!

00:06:59.200 --> 00:07:03.030
Goddamn it!

00:07:08.660 --> 00:07:09.660
Look!

00:07:11.210 --> 00:07:13.780
The heck is that?

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:15.690
Beta?

00:07:21.430 --> 00:07:25.100
It seems Jinkoku-sha have escaped
the island along with your troops.

00:07:25.100 --> 00:07:26.250
That's good.

00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:29.120
Do you have a way to stop that thing?

00:07:29.120 --> 00:07:32.550
Our President has authorized the use 
of nuclear weapons if needed.

00:07:33.040 --> 00:07:38.390
If you're out of options, 
we're going to have to do what we do best.

00:07:38.930 --> 00:07:42.060
Understood. I shall go with you.

00:07:43.000 --> 00:07:46.230
I have a duty to see 
how this whole thing plays out.

00:07:52.230 --> 00:07:53.780
Auctioneer...

00:08:04.800 --> 00:08:07.110
Am I inside you?

00:08:08.900 --> 00:08:13.220
I'm here to take Number 11, 
just as I said I would.

00:08:13.640 --> 00:08:17.450
Were you trying to make
me complacent with the first shot

00:08:17.450 --> 00:08:20.840
and then take me out with the second?

00:08:21.730 --> 00:08:27.610
I'm going to take all three EX-ARMs you 
put up for auction.

00:08:27.610 --> 00:08:31.480
Number 9 was... "Human Bomber," was it?

00:08:31.480 --> 00:08:37.240
It'll be fun to see everyone in Tokyo cower in fear 
after I turn 'em all into bombs.

00:08:37.820 --> 00:08:42.040
And then, Number 16. 
I wonder what its ability is.

00:08:42.380 --> 00:08:46.310
I can't wait to find out! 
I've never used it before!

00:08:47.040 --> 00:08:52.920
And lastly, my beloved Number 11!

00:08:52.920 --> 00:08:58.760
It feels so super-duper good to make
things disappear into black holes.

00:08:58.760 --> 00:09:04.070
I'll make good use of the EX-ARMs 
and bring the world to its knees.

00:09:07.890 --> 00:09:11.240
I just wish you could've seen it happen.

00:09:13.080 --> 00:09:15.440
But whatever. Let's just get right to it.

00:09:15.440 --> 00:09:17.960
Hands up!

00:09:18.990 --> 00:09:21.240
Wha... What is that?

00:09:21.770 --> 00:09:22.950
Why's Alpha's hand there?

00:09:23.680 --> 00:09:25.620
Where's the EX-ARM?

00:09:25.620 --> 00:09:26.990
How?!

00:09:26.990 --> 00:09:29.560
I also wish I could've seen it happen.

00:09:29.560 --> 00:09:33.470
Seen the moment you get sucked 
into a black hole.

00:09:33.470 --> 00:09:34.380
What?

00:09:35.100 --> 00:09:41.420
I have given Akira all my EX-ARMs.

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:48.680
Number 11 is now literally in his hands!

00:09:54.400 --> 00:09:57.310
No way! Impossible!

00:09:57.310 --> 00:10:01.640
When did Alpha have the time 
to take the EX-ARMs?

00:10:02.040 --> 00:10:08.710
Did you really think I would throw
myself at you without a plan?

00:10:08.710 --> 00:10:14.210
Wait, no... Was it Number 16?!

00:10:14.210 --> 00:10:17.990
How I've waited for this time to come.

00:10:18.280 --> 00:10:23.740
I'm going to use my entire existence 
to destroy you!

00:10:27.060 --> 00:10:28.730
Auctioneer.

00:10:42.530 --> 00:10:46.170
Hang on, has time stopped?

00:10:46.170 --> 00:10:50.140
That's right. This is Number 16's ability.

00:10:50.140 --> 00:10:57.040
These three meters of space are
currently isolated from the flow of time.

00:10:57.040 --> 00:11:00.830
That's crazy. I didn't know there
was an EX-ARM that could control time.

00:11:00.830 --> 00:11:04.250
Sadly, it's not that powerful.

00:11:04.250 --> 00:11:12.870
All it can do is isolate you 
for a short while.

00:11:13.610 --> 00:11:16.170
So we're still screwed?

00:11:16.170 --> 00:11:21.640
No, we have more than ten minutes 
before this sphere deactivates.

00:11:21.640 --> 00:11:26.820
In that time, 
I'll give you all the EX-ARMs I have.

00:11:26.820 --> 00:11:31.920
I know you can get out by yourself, 
even if we do end up getting swallowed.

00:11:31.920 --> 00:11:36.920
Get out, and use this Number 11 to beat him!

00:11:37.980 --> 00:11:42.790
Beta, I'm gonna destroy you with this!

00:11:49.570 --> 00:11:51.640
Aren't you a spirited one?

00:11:51.640 --> 00:11:59.530
Not sure what Number 16 does, 
but I guess it'll let you fire off another shot now.

00:11:59.530 --> 00:12:04.240
Let me ask you, though. 
Where are you going to aim?

00:12:04.240 --> 00:12:10.350
I know Number 11 by itself 
isn't enough to take me out.

00:12:10.350 --> 00:12:13.840
The black holes it can create 
without Number 12

00:12:13.840 --> 00:12:16.380
cover only two kilometers at best.

00:12:16.950 --> 00:12:20.710
Meanwhile, I've grown 
to more than ten kilometers.

00:12:20.710 --> 00:12:25.210
Do you think you can figure out 
where my core is?

00:12:25.210 --> 00:12:29.770
What are the odds you'll hit it in one shot?

00:12:30.280 --> 00:12:36.310
He's right. Unless we hit the core—
the brain—his body will repair itself.

00:12:38.110 --> 00:12:42.720
Are we out of options? 
Even with Number 11?!

00:12:42.720 --> 00:12:48.120
Can we still not beat that monster?!

00:12:55.000 --> 00:12:58.780
The little bit you fought back 
was pretty enjoyable.

00:12:58.780 --> 00:13:01.340
But you can't stop me anymore.

00:13:02.450 --> 00:13:06.330
It's game over for mankind!

00:13:12.970 --> 00:13:14.980
<b>Illustration by Komi Shinya</b>

00:13:15.100 --> 00:13:20.400
<b>Tokyo Bay Megafloat</b>

00:13:15.100 --> 00:13:20.400
<b>Unknown Apparition in Tokyo Bay</b>

00:13:15.100 --> 00:13:20.400
<b>Breaking</b>

00:13:15.100 --> 00:13:20.400
<b>Massive Unknown Creature Appears?!</b>

00:13:15.360 --> 00:13:19.390
Uh. We're coming to you live 
from Tokyo Megafloat.

00:13:19.390 --> 00:13:21.610
Do you see this?

00:13:21.610 --> 00:13:24.400
Traffic jam due to a terror attack? 
This sucks.

00:13:24.760 --> 00:13:27.910
Daddy, look, a monster.

00:13:28.320 --> 00:13:30.410
Hey, is that it?

00:13:30.410 --> 00:13:32.170
<i>Do you see this?</i>

00:13:36.600 --> 00:13:38.060
How does it feel?

00:13:38.060 --> 00:13:44.110
Everything you've done your whole life, 
your whole existence, will be erased.

00:13:44.110 --> 00:13:46.170
Victory is mine.

00:13:48.550 --> 00:13:49.860
Wrong.

00:13:51.730 --> 00:13:55.040
You're the one whose
existence will be erased.

00:13:55.040 --> 00:13:59.770
You're going to tell everyone 
where you're hiding.

00:14:00.190 --> 00:14:02.890
I will give my life to reveal all!

00:14:03.530 --> 00:14:06.360
Wait, that's Number 9?!

00:14:09.800 --> 00:14:15.330
Okay. Use Number 9 to turn me 
into a bomb as planned.

00:14:15.330 --> 00:14:17.280
Are you sure about this?

00:14:17.280 --> 00:14:22.170
I told you. We need to do this 
to locate Beta's brain.

00:14:22.170 --> 00:14:29.680
To take him out, we must find out for sure 
where in this massive body his brain is.

00:14:30.370 --> 00:14:34.010
But... you're no different from Bro!

00:14:37.590 --> 00:14:40.300
I can't kill my own brother.

00:14:40.300 --> 00:14:45.680
Don't worry. I was created 
for the sole purpose of destroying Beta.

00:14:45.680 --> 00:14:49.030
You might be fine with that, 
but it'll hurt me!

00:14:49.460 --> 00:14:52.860
I wanna protect, not fight.

00:14:52.860 --> 00:14:56.880
You may be a clone, but I'm a machine, too.

00:14:56.880 --> 00:15:02.880
Even I'd lost sight of 
whether I was human or machine.

00:15:03.370 --> 00:15:12.300
How sad that what Natsume Shuichi did 
to help you actually made you suffer.

00:15:12.970 --> 00:15:17.290
Still, Natsume Akira, you are human.

00:15:17.290 --> 00:15:24.790
Your desire to protect is proof 
of your humanity.

00:15:25.870 --> 00:15:31.100
I'm just a clone that's carrying
on your brother's will.

00:15:32.080 --> 00:15:35.400
I didn't inherit everything of his.

00:15:36.160 --> 00:15:42.250
But I can say that Natsume Shuichi is content 
just knowing you have that desire.

00:15:43.220 --> 00:15:44.550
Bro...

00:15:49.380 --> 00:15:56.180
Come. Let us end the tragic cycle 
that's made people across the world suffer.

00:15:57.520 --> 00:16:02.020
Fight in order to protect everything, 
Natsume Akira!

00:16:02.640 --> 00:16:07.320
I used every second of what
little time I had to destroy him!

00:16:07.320 --> 00:16:09.690
Don't let my life be in vain!

00:16:09.690 --> 00:16:10.680
Okay, got it.

00:16:16.020 --> 00:16:17.450
This is how it should be.

00:16:17.870 --> 00:16:22.370
Don't hesitate. 
Put your best foot forward, Akira.

00:16:23.200 --> 00:16:24.260
Akira.

00:16:26.210 --> 00:16:29.070
You've just gotta put your best foot forward.

00:16:29.070 --> 00:16:31.300
If you want to change, that is.

00:16:35.120 --> 00:16:38.300
I'm going to do just that, Bro!

00:16:45.100 --> 00:16:49.950
Blowing yourself up won't do anything to me!

00:16:49.950 --> 00:16:51.940
Do it, Akira!

00:17:04.650 --> 00:17:05.630
Now!

00:17:05.630 --> 00:17:10.090
Alisa, analyze the merging pattern 
of the damaged part!

00:17:10.090 --> 00:17:11.590
Akira?

00:17:11.590 --> 00:17:16.060
<i>He'll absorb matter from the part 
closest to his core!</i>

00:17:16.590 --> 00:17:19.530
Right. That makes sense.

00:17:23.650 --> 00:17:30.030
If we can decipher that pattern, 
we should be able to locate the core.

00:17:30.030 --> 00:17:34.280
That was the plan Auctioneer—
my bro—came up with!

00:17:34.670 --> 00:17:35.610
It worked.

00:17:36.160 --> 00:17:37.510
Point located.

00:17:39.480 --> 00:17:41.770
<i>Sending you the coordinates, Akira.</i>

00:17:41.770 --> 00:17:42.870
Roger!

00:17:46.660 --> 00:17:48.040
There you are!

00:17:50.120 --> 00:17:54.680
You blew yourself up? 
Did you get desperate, Auctioneer?

00:17:54.680 --> 00:17:57.180
You died for nothing.

00:17:57.180 --> 00:17:59.470
I'll just kill Alpha now.

00:17:59.890 --> 00:18:03.980
EX-ARM Number 11, boot up!

00:18:05.410 --> 00:18:07.530
It's over, Beta!

00:18:13.770 --> 00:18:16.440
Huh? No way...

00:18:16.440 --> 00:18:18.970
How did you know?!

00:18:24.230 --> 00:18:26.830
This is the end, Beta!

00:18:26.830 --> 00:18:30.840
Don't! I'm Number 00, just like you!

00:18:30.840 --> 00:18:34.330
Shut up! I'm not like you!

00:18:34.330 --> 00:18:37.660
But, as a fellow Number 00,

00:18:38.480 --> 00:18:45.400
I'm going to put an end 
to all the tragedy you've caused!

00:18:47.330 --> 00:18:52.310
I would never go down to you... 
to you people!

00:18:52.900 --> 00:18:56.320
This is it for you and me!

00:18:56.320 --> 00:18:58.780
S-Stop!

00:18:58.780 --> 00:19:01.350
No!

00:19:03.140 --> 00:19:09.100
Go face all the people you killed!

00:19:50.930 --> 00:19:52.670
Minami!

00:19:54.340 --> 00:19:55.870
Is it over?

00:19:55.870 --> 00:19:58.550
Yeah. My dear won.

00:20:01.020 --> 00:20:05.350
Thank goodness. Good job, Akira.

00:20:05.350 --> 00:20:08.840
Both energy and heat readings lost.

00:20:08.840 --> 00:20:11.180
So it's really over?

00:20:11.560 --> 00:20:15.690
Beta was completely sucked 
into that black hole.

00:20:16.030 --> 00:20:19.560
<i>Indeed. Beta is gone from this world now.</i>

00:20:19.560 --> 00:20:21.690
<i>Well done, Number 00.</i>

00:20:21.690 --> 00:20:24.840
<i>No, Natsume Akira!</i>

00:20:25.240 --> 00:20:27.290
Yeah!

00:20:32.620 --> 00:20:33.800
Alma.

00:20:33.800 --> 00:20:34.960
Minami.

00:20:34.960 --> 00:20:37.880
I'm so glad you're okay!

00:20:39.260 --> 00:20:42.790
I am, but...

00:20:46.900 --> 00:20:49.920
I'm sorry. I killed Soma.

00:20:49.920 --> 00:20:56.250
No, I made you do something 
that I should've done myself.

00:20:56.930 --> 00:20:57.810
Sorry.

00:21:04.700 --> 00:21:07.560
<i>Bro, Auctioneer...</i>

00:21:09.080 --> 00:21:10.950
<i>Did you see that?</i>

00:21:11.420 --> 00:21:13.960
<i>I avenged you both!</i>

00:21:24.000 --> 00:21:32.440
<i>Th-That massive machine that showed
up earlier has suddenly stopped moving.</i>

00:21:32.440 --> 00:21:34.870
<i>What was that all about?</i>

00:23:22.790 --> 00:23:26.030
Hmph. That Natsume Akira really did it.

00:23:26.030 --> 00:23:27.630
<i>Entering landing sequence.</i>

00:23:28.310 --> 00:23:32.710
Th-The controls aren't working! Come in, HQ!

00:23:40.660 --> 00:23:45.550
Man, I never even imagined 
the world would come to this.

00:23:45.550 --> 00:23:49.200
But I'm the only one now 
who can save Earth, right?

00:23:49.200 --> 00:23:52.830
Next time on <i>EX-ARM:</i> 
"Battle 012 - A Giant Leap."

00:23:50.610 --> 00:23:54.990
<b>A Giant Leap</b>

00:23:52.830 --> 00:23:54.660
I know we'll meet again.
